{
    "$schema": "https://novig.co/schemas/signing-vectors/v1",
    "spec_version": "NOVIG-V3",
    "description": "NOVIG-V3 string-to-sign specification and committed test vectors. Both the Rust and Nest signing stacks test against this file. It is also the source that the Mintlify docs publish verbatim.",
    "string_to_sign_rules": {
        "format": "Six lines joined by LF (U+000A, byte 0x0A), no trailing newline:\n  line 1: NOVIG-V3\n  line 2: {unix_millis} — unpadded decimal, same value as Novig-Timestamp\n  line 3: {METHOD} — uppercase ASCII\n  line 4: {path} — with leading /, sent verbatim, never normalised\n  line 5: {canonical_query} — see below; empty string when no query\n  line 6: {lowercase_hex(sha256(raw_body))} — lowercase hex",
        "canonical_query": "1. Split the raw query string on '&'.\n2. For each pair: split at the FIRST '=' only. The substring before the first '='\n   is the name; the substring after is the value. If no '=' is present, the name\n   is the whole token and the value is the empty string. This means a value that\n   itself contains '=' (e.g. a base64 string 'abc=') is preserved correctly.\n3. Call URI-decode on each part, interpreting percent-encoded sequences\n   as UTF-8. A bare '+' is NOT decoded as a space — RFC 3986 does not give '+'\n   special meaning in query strings. Only '%XX' sequences are decoded.\n4. Re-encode each decoded part: keep RFC 3986 unreserved characters\n   (ALPHA DIGIT - . _ ~) unchanged; encode everything else as %XX with\n   UPPERCASE hex digits.\n5. Sort the encoded pairs bytewise: first by encoded name, then by encoded\n   value as a tiebreaker (relevant when the same name appears more than once).\n6. Join with '&'.\n7. When no query string is present, the canonical query is the empty string,\n   producing an empty line 5. The line is never omitted.",
        "divergence_points": {
            "absent_query": "When no query string is present, line 5 is an empty string. The line must appear; it is never omitted from the string to sign.",
            "empty_body": "An absent or empty body hashes to e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855. The literal string '{}' produces a different hash.",
            "plus_vs_percent20": "Spaces must be encoded as %20, not as '+'. A '+' in the input is treated as a literal '+' and re-encoded as %2B.",
            "hex_case": "Percent-encoding in the canonical query always uses uppercase hex (e.g., %2F not %2f). The body hash always uses lowercase hex.",
            "sort_by_name_then_value": "Query parameters are sorted bytewise by encoded name, then by encoded value. When the same name appears more than once, all occurrences are preserved and sorted by their value. The sort is never by name only.",
            "duplicate_query_params": "When a parameter name appears more than once, all occurrences are preserved in the canonical query. None are dropped or merged.",
            "trailing_slash": "The path is included exactly as sent. A trailing slash is never added or removed. /api/orders and /api/orders/ produce different string to signs.",
            "path_not_decoded": "The path is never percent-decoded before canonicalization. /api/v1/items/foo%2Fbar is not the same as /api/v1/items/foo/bar.",
            "non_ascii_value": "Non-ASCII query values are percent-encoded as their UTF-8 byte sequences with uppercase hex. For example, ü (U+00FC) encodes as %C3%BC.",
            "equals_in_query_value": "A '=' character inside a query value is encoded as '%3D' in the canonical form. Split each pair at the FIRST '=' only; any subsequent '=' belongs to the value. Example: 'token=abc=' → name 'token', value 'abc=', canonical 'token=abc%3D'.",
            "bare_query_param": "A query token with no '=' (e.g. '?flag') has name equal to the whole token and value equal to the empty string. Canonical form: 'flag='."
        }
    },
    "headers": {
        "Novig-Key-Id": "The key's UUID. Not included in the string to sign.",
        "Novig-Timestamp": "Unix time in milliseconds, as an unpadded decimal integer. Accepted clock skew is ±30 seconds.",
        "Novig-Signature": "Standard padded base64 of the raw signature bytes. For Ed25519: the 64-byte output of the Ed25519 signing operation. For ECDSA P-256: sign the string to sign with ECDSA using the P-256 curve and the SHA-256 hash function (i.e. ES256 / prime256v1 + SHA-256). The output is the DER-encoded ASN.1 SEQUENCE of two INTEGERs (r, s), as produced by OpenSSL and Node.js crypto.sign('SHA256', data, ecKey). The DER signature length varies (typically 70–72 bytes); this is expected."
    },
    "algorithm_note": "The client never sends the algorithm in the request. The verifier reads it from the stored key row. This prevents algorithm-confusion attacks (analogous to the JWT alg:none class).",
